IELTS.lesson({"test": 6, "part": 1, "title": "Test 6, Part 1 — the interview", "candidate": "samir", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "Good morning. Come in, have a seat.", "ar": "صباح الخير. تفضّل بالدخول واجلس.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1b2def3fa2b0b362.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "My name is Mohamad Khorbatli. Can you tell me your full name, please?", "ar": "اسمي محمد خرباطلي. هل يمكنك أن تخبرني باسمك الكامل من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c756d0707f344069.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Samir Othman.", "ar": "سمير عثمان.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c66347006ccee4f3.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "And what can I call you?", "ar": "وبماذا أناديك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5085ae49113e09cf.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Samir is fine.", "ar": "سمير تكفي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a46cccf93a61f0e1.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you, Samir. Can I see your identification, please?", "ar": "شكراً لك يا سمير. هل يمكنني رؤية هويّتك من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/959a5972e556f391.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Of course. Here you are.", "ar": "بالتأكيد. تفضّل.", "shot": null, "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/b398597e85e8fd36.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That's all fine.", "ar": "شكراً. كل شيء على ما يرام.", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a65ff8d3eccec277.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now, in this first part I'd like to ask you some questions about yourself. Let's talk about family.", "ar": "الآن، في هذا الجزء الأول أودّ أن أطرح عليك بعض الأسئلة عنك. لنتحدّث عن العائلة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/46e436da696eebd1.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you have a large family?", "ar": "هل عائلتك كبيرة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/6b8aaeb9edc72981.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "By the standards of my generation, no. By my father's, almost comically small. He was one of seven and I've got two children, which is most of the story. You see, the whole arithmetic of a family changed in about forty years and nobody announced it.", "ar": "بمقاييس جيلي، لا. وبمقاييس جيل أبي، صغيرة إلى حدّ يدعو للضحك تقريباً. كان واحداً من سبعة ولديّ أنا ولدان، وهذا معظم القصّة. انظر، حساب العائلة كلّه تغيّر في نحو أربعين سنة ولم يعلن أحد عن ذلك.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4028e7d05ec79f71.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you spend much time with your family?", "ar": "هل تقضي وقتاً طويلاً مع عائلتك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/d507269ab8b5f718.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "More than I did, and that's deliberate. I spent about fifteen years being the teacher who was always at the school in Damascus, marking, extra lessons, the lot, and I've slowly come round to the view that, honestly, nobody has ever thanked a man for the hours he wasn't at home.", "ar": "أكثر مما كنت، وهذا عن قصد. قضيت نحو خمس عشرة سنة وأنا المعلّم الموجود دائماً في المدرسة في دمشق، تصحيح ودروس إضافيّة وكلّ ذلك، ثمّ وصلت ببطء إلى قناعة أنّه، بصراحة، لم يشكر أحدٌ رجلاً يوماً على الساعات التي لم يكن فيها في بيته.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/264b231b0947d0c6.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Who are you closest to in your family?", "ar": "من الأقرب إليك في عائلتك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/d30e7d3759e0dfb8.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "My younger daughter, though I'd never say that in the house. She argues with me, which the other one doesn't, and, well, let me put it this way. I've spent thirty years teaching teenagers in Damascus, and the ones who argued were always the ones I remembered.", "ar": "ابنتي الصغرى، مع أنّني لن أقول ذلك في البيت أبداً. هي تجادلني، والأخرى لا تفعل، و، حسناً، دعني أقولها هكذا. قضيت ثلاثين سنة أعلّم المراهقين في دمشق، والذين كانوا يجادلون هم دائماً من أتذكّرهم.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/fd176d8547a6a046.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Are family relationships changing in your country?", "ar": "هل تتغيّر العلاقات العائليّة في بلدك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/258b63a07a390516.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Loosening, I'd say. I don't think that's the same as weakening. People are further apart and in touch far more often. Whether a daily voice message is worth less than a cousin two streets away in Damascus, I genuinely don't know, and nor does anybody who says they do.", "ar": "أقول إنّها ترتخي. ولا أظنّ أنّ ذلك هو نفسه أن تضعف. الناس أبعد عن بعضهم وعلى تواصل أكثر بكثير. أمّا هل تساوي رسالة صوتيّة يوميّة أقلّ من ابن عمّ على بعد شارعين في دمشق، فأنا حقّاً لا أعرف، ولا يعرف ذلك من يقول إنّه يعرفه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f1ce10e7646a9e98.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's move on to talk about friends.", "ar": "لننتقل للحديث عن الأصدقاء.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/19a884287d55514a.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How often do you see your friends?", "ar": "كم مرّة ترى أصدقاءك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/96cdb63e09343acc.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Thursday evenings, almost without fail, which has survived about twenty-five years and, I think, several things that should have ended it. Four of us, in the same place off the souk. We've run out of new conversation entirely and it doesn't seem to matter at all.", "ar": "مساء كلّ خميس، دون انقطاع تقريباً، وهذا صمد نحو خمس وعشرين سنة، وصمد في رأيي أمام أمور عدّة كان يُفترض أن تنهيه. نحن أربعة، في المكان نفسه قرب السوق. لم يبقَ لدينا حديث جديد إطلاقاً ولا يبدو أنّ لذلك أيّ أهمّية.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/8e17de22bc5f7927.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you prefer a few close friends or a large group?", "ar": "هل تفضّل عدداً قليلاً من الأصدقاء المقرّبين أم مجموعة كبيرة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/ab88b0bd832104cb.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "A few, and I suspect that's age talking and not character. At twenty I'd have given you a different answer with great confidence. Having said that, I notice my daughters at university have thirty friends each and seem no less attached to any of them, so I may simply be describing my own limits.", "ar": "قليلون، وأشكّ أنّ هذا هو العمر يتكلّم لا الطبع. في العشرين كنت سأعطيك جواباً مختلفاً بثقة كبيرة. ومع ذلك، ألاحظ أنّ ابنتيّ في الجامعة لكلّ واحدة منهما ثلاثون صديقاً ولا تبدوان أقلّ تعلّقاً بأيّ منهم، فلعلّي أصف حدودي أنا فحسب.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/8c47e598c251095f.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is it easy to make friends in your city?", "ar": "هل من السهل تكوين صداقات في مدينتك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/93597534eacc59c5.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Easy to meet people, harder to make friends, and I'd say what's short is time, not goodwill. Friends here used to be made by living near each other. The same street in Damascus, the same school, forty years. Nobody's got that any more, so it has to be done on purpose, and most adults aren't very good at doing anything on purpose.", "ar": "من السهل أن تلتقي الناس، ومن الأصعب أن تصنع صداقة، وأقول إنّ ما ينقص هو الوقت لا النيّة الطيّبة. الأصدقاء هنا كانوا يُصنعون بالسكن قرب بعضهم. الشارع نفسه في دمشق، والمدرسة نفسها، وأربعون سنة. لم يعد ذلك متاحاً لأحد، فصار لا بدّ أن يُفعل عن قصد، ومعظم الكبار ليسوا بارعين في فعل أيّ شيء عن قصد.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/81eedd70f34e70b7.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Have your friendships changed over the years?", "ar": "هل تغيّرت صداقاتك على مرّ السنين؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/77e0ea391808e954.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "The ones that lasted became much less about anything. When we were young we were friends over football, over politics, over a hundred things. Now we're friends in Damascus over having been friends, which sounds thin and it's in fact the only kind that survives.", "ar": "التي استمرّت صارت أقلّ ارتباطاً بأيّ موضوع. حين كنّا شباباً كنّا أصدقاء على كرة القدم، وعلى السياسة، وعلى مئة شيء. الآن نحن أصدقاء في دمشق على أنّنا كنّا أصدقاء، وهذا يبدو ضعيفاً وهو في الحقيقة النوع الوحيد الذي يصمد.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/7f1b3382e44c0c1e.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Finally in this part, let's talk about letters and messages.", "ar": "وأخيراً في هذا الجزء، لنتحدّث عن الرسائل.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/37f01c1783187cdc.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you often write letters or emails?", "ar": "هل تكتب رسائل أو بريداً إلكترونياً كثيراً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a51e42517aa47aba.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Emails constantly, letters never, and I notice that I mourn the second more than it deserves. You see, I've got about four letters from my father and nothing at all from anyone who's still alive.", "ar": "بريداً إلكترونياً باستمرار، ورسائل أبداً، وألاحظ أنّني أحزن على الثانية أكثر مما تستحقّ. انظر، عندي نحو أربع رسائل من أبي ولا شيء إطلاقاً من أيّ شخص ما زال حيّاً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/020fbb66821631d7.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you prefer to phone people or to message them?", "ar": "هل تفضّل أن تتّصل بالناس أم أن ترسل لهم رسالة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/d17580cbf21366f4.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Message, which I'd have found unthinkable at thirty. A message lets the other person answer when they're ready, and, you see, let me put it this way. Most of what I say isn't urgent enough to interrupt a man's afternoon in Damascus.", "ar": "رسالة، وهذا ما كنت سأجده غير معقول في الثلاثين. الرسالة تتيح للطرف الآخر أن يجيب حين يكون مستعدّاً، و، انظر، دعني أقولها هكذا. معظم ما أقوله ليس مستعجلاً بما يكفي لأقطع على رجل في دمشق بعد ظهره.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a0590721b098f8b8.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Have you kept any letters you received?", "ar": "هل احتفظت بأيّ رسائل وصلتك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/ca963d8db8339023.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Four, in a drawer in Damascus, and I've read none of them for about a decade. Having said that, I know precisely where they are, which probably suggests the reading isn't the point.", "ar": "أربع، في درج في دمشق، ولم أقرأ أيّاً منها منذ نحو عشر سنوات. ومع ذلك، أعرف تماماً أين هي، وهذا على الأرجح يدلّ على أنّ القراءة ليست هي المقصد.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/614041caeed3cb8b.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Will people still write letters in the future?", "ar": "هل سيظلّ الناس يكتبون الرسائل في المستقبل؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/e5d870a46f7b0c5e.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "As something you do, I'd say, and not as something you use. The practical job has gone elsewhere permanently. What survives will be the part that was never about delivering information in the first place, the way a card at a wedding in Damascus isn't really a card.", "ar": "بوصفها شيئاً تفعله، كما أقول، لا شيئاً تستعمله. الوظيفة العمليّة انتقلت إلى مكان آخر نهائياً. وما سيبقى هو الجزء الذي لم يكن يوماً عن إيصال معلومة، مثلما أنّ البطاقة في عرس في دمشق ليست بطاقة في الحقيقة.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c93bcd737c66580c.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of Part One.", "ar": "شكراً لك. بهذا ينتهي القسم الأول.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/50f379466faf1658.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "Do you have a large family?", "ar": null, "topic": "Family", "model": "By the standards of my generation, no. By my father's, almost comically small. He was one of seven and I've got two children, which is most of the story. You see, the whole arithmetic of a family changed in about forty years and nobody announced it.", "why": "Two standards, two answers, and a generalisation earned by the numbers underneath it."}, {"q": "Do you spend much time with your family?", "ar": null, "topic": "Family", "model": "More than I did, and that's deliberate. I spent about fifteen years being the teacher who was always at the school in Damascus, marking, extra lessons, the lot, and I've slowly come round to the view that, honestly, nobody has ever thanked a man for the hours he wasn't at home.", "why": "A long self-correction with the evidence in the middle of it. The last clause is the whole of what he learned."}, {"q": "Who are you closest to in your family?", "ar": null, "topic": "Family", "model": "My younger daughter, though I'd never say that in the house. She argues with me, which the other one doesn't, and, well, let me put it this way. I've spent thirty years teaching teenagers in Damascus, and the ones who argued were always the ones I remembered.", "why": "Says the unsayable thing and immediately guards it. 'The ones who argued were the ones I remembered' turns a confession into an observation."}, {"q": "Are family relationships changing in your country?", "ar": null, "topic": "Family", "model": "Loosening, I'd say. I don't think that's the same as weakening. People are further apart and in touch far more often. Whether a daily voice message is worth less than a cousin two streets away in Damascus, I genuinely don't know, and nor does anybody who says they do.", "why": "Makes the distinction in two sentences instead of one, which is how a speaker makes it, then refuses to settle a question he thinks is open."}, {"q": "How often do you see your friends?", "ar": null, "topic": "Friends", "model": "Thursday evenings, almost without fail, which has survived about twenty-five years and, I think, several things that should have ended it. Four of us, in the same place off the souk. We've run out of new conversation entirely and it doesn't seem to matter at all.", "why": "A fixed point with a duration on it, and a last clause that is almost the definition of an old friendship."}, {"q": "Do you prefer a few close friends or a large group?", "ar": null, "topic": "Friends", "model": "A few, and I suspect that's age talking and not character. At twenty I'd have given you a different answer with great confidence. Having said that, I notice my daughters at university have thirty friends each and seem no less attached to any of them, so I may simply be describing my own limits.", "why": "Doubts his own answer, checks it against his daughters, and leaves it doubted."}, {"q": "Is it easy to make friends in your city?", "ar": null, "topic": "Friends", "model": "Easy to meet people, harder to make friends, and I'd say what's short is time, not goodwill. Friends here used to be made by living near each other. The same street in Damascus, the same school, forty years. Nobody's got that any more, so it has to be done on purpose, and most adults aren't very good at doing anything on purpose.", "why": "Separates the excuse from the cause in plain words, then supplies the mechanism: the street, the school, forty years."}, {"q": "Have your friendships changed over the years?", "ar": null, "topic": "Friends", "model": "The ones that lasted became much less about anything. When we were young we were friends over football, over politics, over a hundred things. Now we're friends in Damascus over having been friends, which sounds thin and it's in fact the only kind that survives.", "why": "Lands on a paradox and does not explain it. 'friends in Damascus over having been friends' is the answer and he knows it."}, {"q": "Do you often write letters or emails?", "ar": null, "topic": "Letters and messages", "model": "Emails constantly, letters never, and I notice that I mourn the second more than it deserves. You see, I've got about four letters from my father and nothing at all from anyone who's still alive.", "why": "Two frequencies, then a private admission with a number behind it."}, {"q": "Do you prefer to phone people or to message them?", "ar": null, "topic": "Letters and messages", "model": "Message, which I'd have found unthinkable at thirty. A message lets the other person answer when they're ready, and, you see, let me put it this way. Most of what I say isn't urgent enough to interrupt a man's afternoon in Damascus.", "why": "Gives the reason as a courtesy to the other person, which is characteristic of him."}, {"q": "Have you kept any letters you received?", "ar": null, "topic": "Letters and messages", "model": "Four, in a drawer in Damascus, and I've read none of them for about a decade. Having said that, I know precisely where they are, which probably suggests the reading isn't the point.", "why": "A precise number, a precise place, and a conclusion drawn against himself."}, {"q": "Will people still write letters in the future?", "ar": null, "topic": "Letters and messages", "model": "As something you do, I'd say, and not as something you use. The practical job has gone elsewhere permanently. What survives will be the part that was never about delivering information in the first place, the way a card at a wedding in Damascus isn't really a card.", "why": "Speculates without pretending to know, and ends on the one comparison that makes the point without decorating it."}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-joe-medium-s119"}});
